<title>BELGIUM: Generale Bank H1 96 group net up 8.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Generale Bank H1 96 group net up 8.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1995</p>
<p>(billions Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)	   7.31 vs	6.73</p>
<p>Earnings per share (annual basis)* 975 francs vs 900 francs</p>
<p>    Gross income				   69.61 vs     57.02</p>
<p>    Gross profit				   30.18 vs     22.83</p>
<p>    Depreciation, write-downs, provisions  13.30 vs	9.70</p>
<p>    Own funds				     115    vs    108</p>
<p>    Total assets				5,103    vs  4,356</p>
<p>    Return on equity (in pct)		  13.24 vs     13.08</p>
<p>    Return on assets (pct)			0.30 vs	0.32</p>
<p>    Risk Asset Ratio (pct)		     10.01 vs     10.28</p>
<p>    Tier 1 ratio				    5.30 vs	6.02</p>
<p>NOTE - Generale Bank NV is Belgium's biggest bank. * Without</p>
<p>capital increase.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
